# Half-Life hand grenade, HD rig. Measured by vrcardgen, carded by hand.
#
# Part J: "Take one from the chest. The off hand pulls the pin (`Bone04`
# ring, 139 deg; `Dummy23` in the pin-pull sequence). The grip holds the
# spoon; opening the hand releases it and starts the fuse in full fidelity
# (standard fidelity keeps Half-Life's fuse-from-pin cooking). Throw, lob or
# roll at hand speed; the arc shows where it will land."
#
# ONE CARD, THREE GAME DIRECTORIES. valve_hd, gearbox_hd and bshift_hd all
# ship v_grenade.mdl on the same rig: 51 bones, 8 sequences, and the same
# hash 0x1f4f0c84 in all three, measured. The three files differ in byte
# length - different texture pages - but the fingerprint is the rig, so one
# card binds all three. The SD rigs are NOT this model and decline it: valve
# is 49 bones / 0x6e00f52c, gearbox 47 / 0x497f8c68, bshift 50 / 0x3468eedb.
#
# WHICH IS ALSO WHY THE PLAN'S BONE NAMES ARE NOT HERE. `Bone04` and
# `Dummy23` are the SD rig's names, measured: in valve/models/v_grenade.mdl
# `Dummy22` is the body (34.0% of the mesh), `Dummy23` the pin (2.3%) and
# `Bone04` the ring (4.7%). The HD rig names its four weapon bones outright -
# pine (the body, 43.5%), pin (1.8%), ring (12.6%) and spoon (7.6%) - so this
# card uses those. An SD card is a separate measurement.

weapon v_grenade
match  bones 51  seqs 8  hash 0x1f4f0c84

# The bone every position in this card is measured in - the controls, the
# grab points, the chamber, the ejection port. Nothing recorded it until
# the engine had to place a control in the world to ask whether a thumb is
# near it; the simulator never needed one, because it never works in world
# space. Taken from the generator, which has always called this bone the
# WEAPON BODY and is what measured these numbers in the first place.
body   "pine"

# A GRENADE IS NOT FED, IT IS PREPARED, which is what `thrown` means: no
# joints and no fuse of its own. vr_gun.cpp:159 says so in as many words -
# "the grenade is the exception, and its card declares its own ring and its
# own fuse rather than every other thrown weapon inheriting a pin it has not
# got." Both of those are below. Nothing else about the preset is overridden.
type   thrown

# Three seconds, from dlls/handgrenade.cpp:154 - "alway explode 3 seconds
# after the pin was pulled". The same number either way: in full fidelity the
# three seconds run from the spoon flying rather than from the pin, which is
# Part J's change to WHEN the clock starts, not to how long it is.
fuse   3000

# JOINT 0: THE RING, AND IT IS A HINGE, NOT THE PIN.
#
# vrcardgen offered `pin` as a joint candidate and it is wrong to take it.
# Posing pinpull frame by frame, the pin's centroid does not move at all -
# (-0.25, 0.65, 1.99) in the body's frame - through frame 15 of 25, and then
# on frame 16 it is 1.99 units away and by frame 24 it is 49.92 units away,
# off the bottom of the screen. That is not a joint's travel, that is the pin
# being thrown away once it is out; it is debris from frame 16, the way a
# spent case is. Its 1.8% of the mesh could not be grabbed anyway.
#
# What moves while the pin is still seated is the ring, and it moves purely:
# in every one of the eight sequences the ring's own position channels never
# change by so much as a hundredth, and across pinpull frames 8-15 its
# rotation axis in the body's frame measures (0.01, 1.000, 0.00) every frame.
# A clean hinge about the body's Y, which is the lug the pin sits in.
#
# TRAVEL 1.16 RADIANS - the pull, and only the pull. The ring, against its
# bind pose about that axis: 0.00 deg on frame 7 (the last idle frame), then
# 13.17, 32.06, 45.69, 47.59, 44.24, 44.03, 53.49 and 66.50 deg on frame 15.
# 66.50 deg is 1.1606 rad and the pin is still in its lugs at that instant.
# Past frame 15 the ring keeps turning - 168.92 deg by frame 24 - but it is
# riding on the departing pin, so none of that is this joint's range.
#
# The plan's 139 deg is the census's all-sequence euler maximum and it is not
# this. Measured on this rig, the ring's biggest single-axis excursion with
# the pin still seated is in `holster`, 127.75 deg of tumble as the grenade is
# stowed, on three euler channels at once rather than the one clean axis the
# pull uses. Flourish, not mechanism. The pull is 66.50 deg.
joint 0  bone "ring"  hinge  travel 1.16  rest 0
    # A PIN RING HAS NO RETURN SPRING. Stated as an explicit zero rather than
    # left silent: silence means "use the default for this kind of joint", and
    # that default is a pistol slide's return, which climbed the ring back into
    # the fuse the moment the hand came off it.
    spring 0

    # THE PIN COMES CLEAR AT THE TOP OF THE SWING. Measured: the pin is
    # seated for the whole of frames 8-15 and gone on frame 16, so the real
    # fraction is 1.00 - and a mark at 1.00 can never be crossed, because
    # vr_joint.cpp:101 only counts a crossing once the joint is clear of the
    # mark by VRJ_DETENT_HYST, 3% of travel, on the far side. 0.90 is the
    # highest round fraction a hand can actually get past: it reports at
    # 0.93, which is 61.8 of the measured 66.5 deg. The pin leaving at the
    # very end of the pull is what is being said here.
    #
    # DECLARING THIS IS ALSO HOW THE CARD SAYS IT HAS A PIN. vr_card.cpp
    # derives VRFEED_FL_HAS_PIN and action_joint 0 from a `pin_clear` point
    # rather than having the card state either twice.
    #
    # resist 0.30 is NOT measured off the model - there is nothing in an
    # animation that says how hard a pin is to pull. It is the revolver
    # preset's hammer_cock resist, VRF_PCT(30) in vr_gun.cpp, because a
    # grenade pin is the same kind of thing: a mark you have to mean to
    # cross. Drop it to the default 0 and a brushed ring pulls the pin.
    point pin_clear at 0.90  resist 0.30

    # The ring's vertices centre on (-0.63, 0.70, 1.34) in the body's frame
    # at rest, measured, and reach 0.70 units from that centre. The radius is
    # rounded up to 1.0 so a finger anywhere on the ring counts as on it,
    # which is still barely a third of the grenade's own 2.92-unit width, so
    # a hand on the body is not mistaken for a hand on the ring.
    grab  point -0.63 0.70 1.34  radius 1.0

# THE SPOON IS A CONTROL AND NOT A JOINT, because the model gives it no
# travel to measure. `spoon` owns 68 vertices, 7.6% of the mesh - a strip
# 0.70 x 2.24 x 3.55 running the length of the body, which is the safety
# lever - and it is never animated: zero span on all six channels in all
# eight sequences. There is nothing to measure, and a travel invented here
# would be a number with no source.
#
# It does not need one. The spoon is the one catch in the vocabulary that
# hangs off no joint (vr_card.cpp's single exception, and VRGun_SpoonControl
# in vr_gun.cpp:349): your GRIP is what holds it down, so letting go of the
# grenade releases it with no mechanism in between. The control is only for
# letting it go DELIBERATELY while still holding on - cooking - which is a
# thumb on the lever and a face button, per Part G's table.
#
# `at` is the spoon's own measured vertex centroid in the body's frame.
control spoon  at 0.00 0.38 1.65  finger thumb  kind button

# NO STRIKE LINE, so the parser's weak pistol-whip default stands. Part J
# gives the butt-stroke to firearms; a grenade is not one, and clubbing a
# soldier with a live grenade is not a mechanism this wants to encourage.
#
# NO `fire` LINE either: a grenade has no trigger and no rate. The preset's
# semi-only default trigger is never consulted on a thrown weapon.
#
# AND NOTHING FOR THE BODY. `pine` is the weapon body - 43.5% of the mesh,
# root-parented, and the bone that carries the whole grenade through draw,
# holster and pinpull - so it is the frame every number above is in, not a
# part. The model has no attachments at all, which is correct: a grenade has
# no muzzle. Its vertex extent in its own frame is 2.60 x 2.92 x 4.77 units,
# diagonal 6.17. (vrcardgen's "weapon extent 14.1" is the whole model
# including both arms; the grenade alone is 6.17.)
